SonusGrid aggregates several third-party components. Each is licensed under
its own terms; the following table summarises them.

  Component                       Upstream                                License
  ────────────────────────────    ────────────────────────────────────    ──────────────────────
  SonusGrid Engine (forked)       https://github.com/teodly/inferno       GPLv3-or-later OR
   — see crates/sonusgrid-engine/NOTICE for the fork lineage              AGPLv3-or-later
  Statime (PTP daemon)            https://github.com/teodly/statime       Apache-2.0 OR MIT
                                  (fork of pendulum-project/statime)
  alsa-rs                         https://github.com/diwic/alsa-rs        Apache-2.0 OR MIT
  libpulse-binding (Rust)         https://docs.rs/libpulse-binding        LGPLv2.1+
  PipeWire (server, runtime)      https://pipewire.org/                   MIT
  GTK4 / libadwaita               https://gtk.org/, https://gnome.org/    LGPLv2.1+
  PyGObject                       https://pygobject.gnome.org/            LGPLv2.1+

SonusGrid's own source code (everything under crates/sonus-cli/,
crates/sonusgrid-bridge/, gui/, systemd/, alsa/, packaging/, docs/, tests/)
is licensed under GPLv3-or-later; see COPYING.

The bundled SonusGrid Engine (crates/sonusgrid-engine/) is a fork of Inferno
that makes SonusGrid a derivative work of Inferno and pins the distributed
binary to GPLv3-or-later. See crates/sonusgrid-engine/NOTICE for full
attribution.

Statime and PipeWire are kept as separate processes; their licenses do not
contaminate SonusGrid.

Trademark notice: "Dante" is a trademark of Audinate Pty Ltd. Sonus is not
affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Audinate. The trademark is
referenced solely to describe interoperability.
